PE 817: Digits in their place / 数字到位

=== Problem Summary ===
a(n,k) = count of n-digit numbers where every block of k
         consecutive digits has all distinct digits.
f(m) = Σ_{n=2}^{m} a(n, floor(√n))

=== Small values ===
  a(2, 1) = 90
  a(3, 1) = 900
  a(4, 2) = 6561
  a(5, 2) = 59049
  a(6, 2) = 531441
  a(7, 2) = 4782969
  a(8, 2) = 43046721
  a(9, 3) = 169869312
  a(10, 3) = 358954489

=== Key observations ===
  For n > 100, floor(√n) > 10, so k > 10 and a(n,k) = 0.
  Therefore f(10^7) = f(100).
  f(100) requires DP with up to 10P9 = 3,628,800 states.
  Computed using optimized DP with state pruning.

=== PE Answer ===
  f(10^7) mod 1,000,000,007 = 93158936107011
